{"symbol":"SON.WA","area":"poland","updated":"2026-11-09T19:57:50Z","info":{"address1":"ul. Stanislawa Wokulskiego 11","city":"Swidnica","zip":"58-100","country":"Poland","phone":"48 748 84 10 53","fax":"48 748 58 38 09","website":"https://www.sonel.pl","industry":"Scientific & Technical Instruments","industryKey":"scientific-technical-instruments","industryDisp":"Scientific & Technical Instruments","sector":"Technology","sectorKey":"technology","sectorDisp":"Technology","longBusinessSummary":"Sonel S.A. engages in the production and sale of electronic measuring instruments in Poland. The company offers electrical safety measurements, including multifunctional installation, insulation resistance, earth ground, loop impedance, RCD, PV installation, and EV charging station testers; and power quality analysis, safety of electrical equipment, low resistance measurements, and thermal imagers and pyrometers products, as well as instruments for detecting cables, conductors, and pipes in various environments. It also provides multimeters, clamp meters, voltage testers, phase sequence and motor rotation tester, and distance meters; and measuring sets, illuminance measurements, acoustic testers, leakage current alarm, partial discharge measurements, high voltage equipment, and laboratory and training equipment. In addition, the company offers accessories comprising adapters, clamps, test lead and probes, crocodile clips and cramps, power and batteries, carrying cases and straps, tools, other accessories, shunts, and accessories for thermal imagers and PAT series; and software products. Its products are used for electromobility, photovoltaic, industry and production, energy efficiency, and safety of electrical equipment applications. Sonel S.A. was founded in 1989 and is headquartered in Swidnica, Poland.","fullTimeEmployees":380,"companyOfficers":[{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Tomasz  Wisniewsk","title":"President of the Management Board","exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"